ship culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Nerdy Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $48M market cap on $179M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at -10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 67% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $24M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -370.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 16% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 52% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-10.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 41% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 93/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Financial qu